1]Explain indetail about datatypes in java ?
	
	->In java datatype defines the type of value that a variable is storing and how much memory it is needed
	is called as a datatype in java
	->In java thier are 2 types of datatypes:-
		i]Primitive datatypes
		ii]Non Primitive datatypes
		
Primitive datatypes:-
=====================

	->Primitive datatypes are the most basic datatypes in java
	->Primitive datatypes stores directly in memory and they has predefined size and range
	->Primitive datatypes are most efficient in terms of memory usage and processing speed compared with
	non-primitive datatypes
	
	->In Primitive thier are 8 types:-
		1]boolean : is used to store true or false values
		
		2]char : is used to store single character in single quotes and it occupies 2 bytes in computer
		memory
		
		3]byte : is used to store the integer values from the range -128 to +127 and it occupies 1 byte
		in computer memory
		
		4]short : is used to the integer values from the range -32768 to +32767 and it occupies 2 bytes in
		computer memory
		
		5]int : is used to store more integer values than "short" datatype and it occupies 4 bytes in
		computer memory
		
		
		6]long : is used to store more integer values than "int" datatype and it occupies 8 bytes in
		computer memory,by default the value assigned to long will be treated as int value so we need to
		specify "l" or "L" at suffix place
		
		
		7]float : is used to store the floating point values and it occupies 4 bytes in computer memory
		by default the value assigned to float will be treated as double value so we need to specify "f" or 
		"F" at suffix place
		
		8]double : is used to store floating point values and it occupies 8 bytes in computer memory
		

		float store upto 7 decimal digits of precision 
		double store upto 15 decimal digits of  precision 
		

Non-Primitive datatypes:-
=========================

	->Non-Primitive datatypes is used to store the reference of an object  in stack area and the 
	actually object itself will be created in heap area
	
for an examples: Class,Object,Array,String